WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.780
Welcome to Grade 7 English, Unit 4:
Transport, Cities, and Urban Solutions.

2
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:10.840
In this unit you will explore how cities
grow, how people move through them,

3
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:16.920
and how communities around the world are finding
creative solutions to make urban life better for everyone.

4
00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:24.660
You will read about transport systems, green innovations,
and the challenges that cities face in East Africa and beyond.

5
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:30.360
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

6
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.480
By the end of this unit,

7
00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:38.740
you will be able to read and understand a passage
about city transport and discuss its ideas in English.

8
00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:45.720
You will also use prepositions of time and
place (in, on, at) correctly and confidently.

9
00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:52.100
You will also form the passive voice in the past
simple, present simple, and with modal verbs.

10
00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.860
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

11
00:00:55.400 --> 00:01:03.700
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: construction,
creativity, credibility, differentiation, inequality,

12
00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:04.620
modify.

13
00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:10.700
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

14
00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.380
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

15
00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:22.420
The reading sequence includes Moving Through Mogadishu:
A City in Motion and An Interview About City Transport.

16
00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:24.340
Read actively.

17
00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:29.300
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

18
00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:33.160
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

19
00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:37.740
The first language focus is Prepositions of Time and Place.

20
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:44.040
Prepositions are small but powerful words that show
how the other words in a sentence relate to each other,

21
00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:49.540
and the three most important prepositions
of time and place — in, on and at —

22
00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:53.720
make your English sound natural
and precise when chosen correctly.

23
00:01:54.500 --> 00:02:00.900
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:06.960
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Vocabulary Expert Interview.

25
00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:11.580
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:15.000
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:18.640
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.320
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:26.620
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:29.260
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:37.320
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
